WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.410
With hundreds of shows hitting the small screen
each year, there are bound to be some strange

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.120
ones that slip under the radar - and a few
that will have you wondering how they were

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.930
ever made in the first place.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.110
Here are some of the most bizarre TV shows
you won't believe actually exist.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.119
Vanilla Ice Goes Amish

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:19.830
If you've been hoping to find a TV show in
which a dressed-down Vanilla Ice moves in

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.609
with the Amish, the D.I.Y.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:22.650
Network has got you covered.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.710
In 2013's appropriately titled home-improvement
spin-off Vanilla Ice Goes Amish, the rapper

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.800
assists his Pennsylvania Dutch hosts with
a variety of tasks around the house.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.250
The rest of the time, he basically just sits
on the porch, tells jokes, and does everything

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.329
but embrace the Amish lifestyle.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:40.890
If that isn't good television, what is?

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.429
The Swan

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:46.339
Reality TV has really scraped the bottom of
the barrel a few times — and you'd be hard-pressed

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:51.019
to find a better example than The Swan, a
two-season beauty pageant featuring so-called

00:00:51.019 --> 00:00:56.320
"ugly ducklings" who receive extensive plastic
surgery, life coaching, and psychological

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.320
therapy.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.420
Unsurprisingly, some contestants were left
both physically and emotionally scarred, and

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.650
the show has rightfully been chastised for
exploiting women with pre-existing personal

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.650
issues.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:11.010
No matter which way you try to spin it, The
Swan was ugly, exploitative, and just plain

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.010
awful.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.570
Thankfully, the planned Celebrity Swan revival
never made it to the air.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.440
Ramez in Control

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.900
Egypt's Ramez in Control is like Punk'd on
steroids.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.280
Well-known television prankster Ramez Galal
isn't afraid to take things to the absolute

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.280
extreme.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.610
He once gave socialite Paris Hilton the ride
of her life by staging an emergency airplane

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.540
landing — though speculation has arisen
that she was in on the prank all along.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:39.360
According to CNN, Galal once ran a prank called
Ramez the Desert Fox in which he and a group

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.180
of armed men hijacked a bus before kidnapping
and blindfolding the passengers.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.670
Yikes.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.040
The Puppy Channel

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.380
Long before videos of keyboard playing cats
were only a few clicks away, there was a short-lived

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.420
television pilot called The Puppy Channel.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.890
According to Upvoted, it actually tested well,
too, with 38 percent of one focus group claiming

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.530
they'd probably watch it at least once per
day.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.890
Unfortunately, The Puppy Channel never did
become its own full-fledged channel — but

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.950
at least we still have Puppy Bowl.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:07.950
Sunset Daze

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.670
In 2010, WE TV launched their own geriatric
Jersey Shore in the form of Sunset Daze — a

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.830
reality show featuring baby boomers gone wild.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:21.370
According to the LA Times, the show was a
success among older viewers, but the under-50

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:25.810
demographic found the show's many age-defying
one-liners cheesy, and the first episode's

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.740
discussions regarding going commando struck
many as cringeworthy.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.620
As a result, the show was put out to pasture
after only one season.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.800
Prince of Poets

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.250
Abu Dhabi's competition show Prince of Poets
focuses on wannabe wordsmiths reciting their

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.670
best lines to an enthusiastic crowd and panel
of judges.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:46.880
Unlike the United States, where poets are
largely confined to open-mic nights in coffee

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.220
shops, the Arab world really digs its poetry
— poets in some parts of the Middle East

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.680
are bona fide pop stars, filling stadiums
with eager ears excited to hear some verbal

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:56.950
bliss.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:57.950
Cop Rock

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.920
Have you ever found yourself watching a cop
show like The Shield or Blue Bloods and wishing

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.959
it was actually a musical?

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:04.959
Probably not.

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:09.380
But if you have, definitely check out 1990's
musical police drama Cop Rock.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:13.970
ABC's bizarre cross-genre show only lasted
11 episodes, and has since found its way onto

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:18.150
more than its fair share of "Worst TV Shows
of All Time" lists — but no one can deny

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.770
the fact that the show is a lot of fun to
laugh with and laugh at.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:26.520
The show also deserves credit for trying something
new in the industry full of recycled ideas.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.630
After all, when's the last time you've seen
a singing baby merchant on TV?

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:31.630
The Flying Nun

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.680
It's hard to imagine a major network greenlighting
a show about a flying nun.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.260
What's even harder to believe is that such
a show would make it through more than 80

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:40.260
episodes.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:46.130
The Flying Nun aired on ABC from 1967 to 1970,
and featured Sally Field as a novice nun whose

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:50.180
small frame and stiff cornette made her susceptible
to gusts of wind.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.450
As one might expect, the comedy is fairly
mediocre — in fact, as Field told Oprah

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.940
Winfrey in 2008, she didn't even want to do
the show.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.340
Fortunately, she transcended the ridiculous
role, and went on to enjoy a long, award-filled

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.340
acting career.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.340
Thanks for watching!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.480
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.550
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

